144+  0201              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
145+  0201              ; Guest RAM backing access
146+  0201              ;
147+  0201              ; Guest RAM allocation starts at NeoGS physical page 44h.
148+  0201              ; Guest byte address maps linearly to physical offset 110000h + guest address.
149+  0201              ; WIN3 is a permanently reserved bank aperture; its current page is volatile.
150+  0201              ; These routines do not restore WIN3's previous page because the page port is
151+  0201              ; write-only and WIN3 is owned exclusively by this memory backend.
152+  0201              ;
153+  0201              ; Entry address: x86_phys_addr = low, middle, high-nibble.
154+  0201              ; Read returns byte in A, carry clear. Non-RAM overlay regions return carry.
155+  0201              ; Write takes byte in A, carry clear on success; non-RAM returns carry.
156+  0201              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
