214+  024C              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
215+  024C              ; Unified guest memory interface
216+  024C              ;
217+  024C              ; Guest physical address is classified before selecting its physical backing:
218+  024C              ;   00000-9FFFF / C8000-FDFFF : guest RAM, pages 44h-83h
219+  024C              ;   A0000-BFFFF               : linear VGA aperture backing, pages 30h-37h
220+  024C              ;   C0000-C7FFF               : VGA BIOS slot, pages 20h-21h
221+  024C              ;   FE000-FFFFF               : system BIOS slot, page 10h (8 KiB image)
222+  024C              ;
223+  024C              ; The VGA aperture backend is deliberately a byte-linear staging layer over
224+  024C              ; the first 128 KiB of the 256 KiB VRAM allocation. It is NOT yet IBM VGA
225+  024C              ; plane/latch/read-mode/write-mode emulation. VGA register semantics are a
226+  024C              ; separate implementation stage.
227+  024C              ;
228+  024C              ; All backing is reached through WIN3. A is the page bias for the address
229+  024C              ; formula: page = (guest_high_nibble*4)+(guest_middle>>6)+bias.
230+  024C              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
